Basic STL headers (<optional>, <string>, <vector>) with system libc++.

Reclassified CORE -> KNOWNBUG by the member-typedef conformance fix
([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef]).  Previously this passed only because the
non-conformant *truncated* std::string / std::vector had their operations
havoc'd (symex executed none of the real containers; the properties were
vacuous).  The fix makes the front end conformant and symex now executes the
REAL container machinery, which does not complete within resources.

Second-tier verification-PERFORMANCE item, not a conformance one; the previous
"pass" was unsound.  Reclassify back to CORE once symex is tractable on the real
containers.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
